  "notes": "Benchtop material rules (BENCH-7), research in docs/benchtops.md. Per material and thickness: the overhang past the cabinets that needs no support, how far an 18 mm substrate takes it (0: no such step), support spacing beyond, whether the overhang may be at most a third of the top's depth, and cut-out clearances (from the front and rear edges, between a sink and its tap hole, and an electrical cut-out from a slab's edge). A benchtop takes the entry of its material with the largest thickness not over its own. Engineered stone is banned in Australia since 1 July 2024 and is not offered. Compact laminate and timber wait for sources. Every value is overridable per benchtop. Not verified by a person.",
